+// Speed (same results): whether the smoothing of the areas in setTube() is sure to take the
+// new area as it is, found without the four square roots. The smoothing compares the 4th
+// roots r of the old and the new area: closing is slowed down if r(new) - r(old) < -0.001,
+// opening if r(new) - r(old) > 0.002. For lo = the smaller and hi = the larger of the two
+// areas, r(hi) - r(lo) <= (hi - lo) * r'(lo) = (hi - lo) * r(lo) / (4 * lo), as r' falls, and
+// r(lo) <= bound for lo <= bound^4. So the difference is at most 0.00099 (0.00198) if
+// bound * (hi - lo) <= 0.00396 * lo (0.00792 * lo). The margin of 1 % is far more than the
+// rounding errors of this test and of the roots and their difference in setTube() (below
+// 1e-14 for roots up to 10), so that the difference computed there is sure not to pass
+// its threshold.
+static inline bool smoothingLeavesArea(double oldArea, double newArea)
+{
+  const bool closing = (newArea < oldArea);
+  const double lo = closing ? newArea : oldArea;
+  const double hi = closing ? oldArea : newArea;
+  double bound;
+  if (!(lo > 0.0)) { return false; }
+  if (lo <= 1.0) { bound = 1.0; }
+  else if (lo <= 16.0) { bound = 2.0; }
+  else if (lo <= 10000.0) { bound = 10.0; }
+  else { return false; }
+  return bound * (hi - lo) <= (closing ? 0.00396 : 0.00792) * lo;
+}
